---
name: Ratatouille
description: Classic French ratatouille with eggplant, zucchini, peppers and tomatoes.
---

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a large frying pan.

Slice @onions{350%g} into rings and cut @red and green bell peppers{350%g} into strips. Cook them gently in the oil until softened.

Peel and quarter @ripe tomatoes{500%g}. Chop @garlic{3%cloves}.

Once the onions and peppers are tender, add the tomatoes, garlic, @thyme{1%sprig}, and @bay leaf{1%leaf}.

Season with @salt{} and @black pepper{}. Cover and simmer gently for 45 minutes.

Meanwhile, slice @eggplants{350%g} and @zucchini{350%g} into rounds.

Cook the eggplant and zucchini separately or together in the remaining @olive oil{4%tbsp} for 15 minutes, until tender.

Check that the vegetables are no longer firm. Add the eggplant and zucchini to the tomato mixture and cook over very low heat for another 10 minutes.

Taste and adjust with @salt{} and @black pepper{} if necessary.

Serve hot, or allow to cool and serve cold.
